MISHIMA, IKUHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAKI, AKIRA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TONE, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>WADA, KAZUHITO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YUI, KOJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A thermoplastic resin composition comprising 100 parts by weight of a thermoplastic resin (A) and 1 to 11 parts by weight of graft copolymer particles (B) each comprising a hollow rubber part and a grafting chain, wherein the relative volume of the hollow parts in the hollow rubber part is 1 to 70 % by volume. The impact resistance is further improved by the effect of the hollow parts in the graft copolymer particles.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette composition à base de résine thermoplastique comporte 100 parties par poids d'une résine thermoplastique (A) et de 1 à 11 parties par poids de particules de copolymère greffé (B), comprenant chacune une partie creuse en caoutchouc et une chaîne de greffage. La valeur du volume relatif des parties creuses dans la partie creuse en caoutchouc est comprise entre 1 et 70 % en volume. La résistance aux chocs est encore accrue par l'existence des parties creuses dans les particules de copolymère greffé.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set f